t", "Repayment schedule configuration"], "users": ["Maker", "Checker", "Sanctioner", "Credit", "Operations", "Admin"], "integrations": ["CIBIL", "DMS & CKYC", "Core banking / bank systems", "Payment / collection systems"], "workflow": ["Application", "Checks", "Credit decision", "Sanction", "Disbursement", "Repayment"], "reports": ["Application funnel", "Approval status", "Disbursement status", "Workflow ageing"], "pm": ["Product strategy", "Journey & workflow design", "API / integration requirements", "Business rules", "UAT scenario design", "Client demos"], "api": "/api/v1/loans/applications", "error": "Sanction action unavailable: checker approval is pending.", "learning": "A reusable lending platform needs configurable product rules without losing the controls that make credit workflows auditable."}, {"id": "cms", "name": "CMS", "category": "Payments & Cards", "color": "#ff9fc5", "purpose": "Card management covering personalised and instant cards across major card networks.", "problem": "Card operations require network-aware product configuration, issuance workflows and operational visibility.", "capabilities": ["Personalised cards", "Instant cards", "Card product setup", "RuPay", "Visa", "Mastercard", "NBIN-related issuance context", "Operational reporting"], "users": ["Card Operations", "Maker", "Checker", "Branch User", "Admin"], "integrations": ["NPCI / card ecosystem", "RuPay", "Visa", "Mastercard", "Core banking"], "workflow": ["Request", "Validate", "Network route", "Issue", "Track", "Report"], "reports": ["Issuance status", "Card product summary", "Pending actions", "Operations dashboard"], "pm": ["Integration readiness", "Configuration design", "Exception handling", "API requirements", "Client demos", "UAT"], "api": "/api/v1/cards/requests", "error": "Card request cannot progress: network/product mapping is incomplete.", "learning": "Network-dependent products need configuration, dependency visibility and failure handling as first-class product concerns."}, {"id": "shares", "name": "Shares", "category": "Financial Control", "color": "#a7d8ff", "purpose": "Share and portfolio management with dividend calculation and governance reporting.", "problem": "Share operations need controlled updates, calculations, approvals and reliable management outputs.", "capabilities": ["Share management", "Portfolio management", "Dividend calculation", "Maker-checker", "Board meeting reports", "Operational reporting"], "users": ["Share Manager", "Maker", "Checker", "Finance", "Management"], "integrations": ["Core / finance data", "Document repository", "Reporting layer"], "workflow": ["Capture holding", "Validate", "Calculate", "Approve", "Report", "Board view"], "reports": ["Portfolio summary", "Dividend report", "Shareholding report", "Board meeting pack"], "pm": ["Business-rule mapping", "Workflow controls", "Report specification", "Data validation", "UAT"], "api": "/api/v1/shares/portfolio", "error": "Dividend calculation requires an approved shareholding snapshot.", "learning": "When outputs feed governance forums, calculation integrity and approval lineage become product features."}, {"id": "pm-schemes", "name": "PM Schemes", "category": "Operations", "color": "#9fe3a9", "purpose": "Management of government-launched schemes through configurable operational workflows.", "problem": "Scheme processes evolve and need configurable operational journeys, controls and reporting.", "capabilities": ["Scheme master", "Eligibility / workflow configuration", "Operational tracking", "Status monitoring", "Reports", "User controls"], "users": ["Scheme Operations", "Maker", "Checker", "Branch User", "Admin"], "integrations": ["Bank systems", "Customer / account data", "Reporting layer"], "workflow": ["Scheme setup", "Capture", "Validate", "Process", "Track", "Report"], "reports": ["Scheme status", "Application / beneficiary view", "Pending actions", "Management summary"], "pm": ["Configuration strategy", "Workflow design", "Stakeholder alignment", "Training", "Feedback-driven enhancement"], "api": "/api/v1/schemes", "error": "Scheme processing blocked: mandatory scheme parameters are incomplete.", "learning": "Configuration reduces the need to rebuild the product every time an operational programme changes."}, {"id": "cibil", "name": "CIBIL", "category": "Lending & Credit", "color": "#86c8ff", "purpose": "Credit-information retrieval through API connectivity for lending workflows.", "problem": "Credit decisions depend on timely external credit information and a reliable exception path when the dependency fails.", "capabilities": ["Credit information request", "API connectivity", "Response capture", "Status tracking", "Exception handling", "LOS hand-off"], "users": ["Credit User", "Maker", "Operations", "Admin"], "integrations": ["CIBIL API", "LOS–LMS", "Customer / application data"], "workflow": ["Loan application", "Request credit info", "API response", "Validate", "Attach to decision", "Continue"], "reports": ["Request status", "Response success / failure", "Pending requests", "Credit workflow view"], "pm": ["API requirement definition", "Failure-state design", "Integration testing", "UAT", "Operational readiness"], "api": "/api/v1/credit/cibil/request", "error": "Credit bureau response unavailable. Retry and manual exception handling are required.", "learning": "An integration is not complete when the happy-path API works; timeout, retry, status and recovery are product requirements."}, {"id": "reconciliation", "name": "Reconciliation", "category": "Payments & Cards", "color": "#f4c78e", "purpose": "Transaction reconciliation across AEPS, UPI, Switch, ATM and other transaction streams.", "problem": "Identify matched and unmatched records, manage exceptions and close reconciliation cycles.", "capabilities": ["Transaction ingestion", "Matching / reconciliation", "Exception identification", "Status tracking", "Operational reporting", "Settlement-oriented views"], "users": ["Reconciliation User", "Operations", "Maker", "Checker", "Finance"], "integrations": ["AEPS", "UPI", "Switch", "ATM", "Bank transaction systems"], "workflow": ["Ingest", "Normalise", "Match", "Exception", "Resolve", "Close"], "reports": ["Matched / unmatched", "Exception ageing", "Stream-wise summary", "Daily reconciliation"], "pm": ["Data-flow mapping", "Exception design", "Operational dashboards", "Integration readiness", "UAT"], "api": "/api/v1/reconciliation/transactions", "error": "Record remains unreconciled: source reference and settlement amount differ.", "learning": "Reconciliation is fundamentally an exception-management product; the unresolved queue is as important as the matched count."}, {"id": "aml-kyc", "name": "AML–KYC", "category": "Compliance", "color": "#ffb2a6", "purpose": "Transaction monitoring, rule-based flagging and compliance reporting.", "problem": "Compliance teams need to identify relevant activity, investigate exceptions and produce required reporting with traceability.", "capabilities": ["Transaction monitoring", "Rule-based flagging", "Risk / alert workflow", "CTR reporting", "STR reporting", "NTR reporting", "KYC controls", "Compliance dashboards"], "users": ["Compliance User", "AML Analyst", "Maker", "Checker", "Compliance Manager"], "integrations": ["Transaction sources", "KYC / CKYC", "Bank systems", "Reporting interfaces"], "workflow": ["Transaction", "Rules", "Alert", "Review", "Decision", "Report"], "reports": ["Alerts", "Case ageing", "CTR", "STR", "NTR", "Compliance summary"], "pm": ["Regulatory requirement translation", "Rule / workflow design", "Reporting", "Stakeholder governance", "UAT", "Operational training"], "api": "/api/v1/aml/alerts", "error": "Alert cannot be closed: review disposition and mandatory evidence are missing.", "learning": "Compliance products need traceability: why something was flagged, who reviewed it, what evidence was used and what was reported."}, {"id": "treasury", "name": "Treasury", "category": "Financial Control", "color": "#9ed7ff", "purpose": "Treasury operational workflows supporting BOD and EOD activities.", "problem": "Time-bound treasury activities need clear state transitions, dependencies, controls and closure visibility.", "capabilities": ["BOD activities", "EOD activities", "Operational checklist", "Status tracking", "Exception visibility", "Reporting"], "users": ["Treasury User", "Maker", "Checker", "Treasury Manager", "Admin"], "integrations": ["Core banking / finance systems", "Transaction data", "Reporting layer"], "workflow": ["BOD start", "Validate inputs", "Execute", "Check", "EOD close", "Report"], "reports": ["BOD checklist", "EOD status", "Pending actions", "Treasury summary"], "pm": ["Operational workflow design", "Dependency mapping", "Exception paths", "Release readiness", "Client feedback"], "api": "/api/v1/treasury/eod", "error": "EOD close blocked: a mandatory reconciliation / validation task is still open.", "learning": "Time-bound operational products need strong guardrails before a cycle can be closed."}, {"id": "dms-ckyc", "name": "DMS & CKYC", "category": "Compliance", "color": "#c2b0ff", "purpose": "Document management and CKYC workflows covering OVD, verification, secure storage and CKYC retrieval.", "problem": "KYC processes require complete customer information, authentic documents, controlled access and reliable retrieval.", "capabilities": ["OVD capture", "Customer information", "Document authenticity verification", "Secure storage", "CKYC number retrieval", "Document status"], "users": ["KYC User", "Maker", "Checker", "Compliance", "Admin"], "integrations": ["CKYC", "Customer / account systems", "LOS–LMS", "Document services"], "workflow": ["Capture", "Validate", "Verify", "Store", "Retrieve CKYC", "Share status"], "reports": ["KYC status", "Document completeness", "Verification exceptions", "CKYC lookup status"], "pm": ["Data model", "API integration", "Security considerations", "Edge-case design", "UAT", "Training"], "api": "/api/v1/ckyc/search", "error": "Document rejected: authenticity or mandatory metadata validation failed.", "learning": "Document products need lifecycle, metadata, permissions and verification—not simply file upload."}];

const filters = ['All', 'Lending', 'Payments & Cards', 'Compliance', 'Financial Control', 'Governance', 'Operations'];
const outcomePrinciples = [
  ['Standardise', 'Reusable platform patterns'],
  ['Configure', 'Institution-specific workflows'],
  ['Integrate', 'Existing financial ecosystem'],
  ['Adopt', 'Migration, deployment & enablement'],
];
---

<ProjectShell
  title="Integrated Channels Suite"
  previous={{ title: 'Telecom Analytics & Cost Optimization', href: '/projects/telecom-cost-optimization' }}
  next={{ title: 'Ayu DocConnect', href: '/projects/ayu-docconnect' }}
  navSections={navSections}
  ctaText="View Projects"
  ctaHref="/#portfolio"
  showProjectFooter={false}
  viewportFitPrototype={true}
>
  <main class="ics-case">
    <section class="ics-section ics-overview" id="overview" aria-labelledby="ics-overview-title">
      <div class="ics-inner">
        <div class="ics-section-kicker"><i></i><span>DIGITAL BANKING PLATFORM · END-TO-END PRODUCT OWNERSHIP</span><b>M2P FINTECH</b></div>
        <div class="ics-overview-main">
          <div class="ics-overview-copy">
            <p class="ics-overline">Product case study · Banks &amp; NBFCs</p>
            <h1 id="ics-overview-title">Integrated Channels Suite</h1>
            <p class="ics-lede">I led product management for a digital banking platform for banks and NBFCs, built from scratch as a reusable 12-application suite, bringing together lending, cards, payments, reconciliation, compliance, treasury, audit, assets, GST, shares, government schemes, credit bureau connectivity and document/KYC workflows - while supporting configurable journeys, controls, integrations and implementation at client sites.</p>
            <div class="ics-overview-actions"><a href="#challenge">Start the case study <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a href="#portfolio">Explore the products <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="#tech-data">See ecosystem architecture</a></div>
          </div>
          <aside class="ics-glance" aria-label="Product at a glance">
            <div class="ics-glance-title"><img src="/profile/m2p-logo.svg" alt="M2P Fintech" /><div><small>M2P FINTECH · PRODUCT CASE STUDY</small><h2>Product at a glance</h2></div></div>
            <div class="ics-glance-list">
              <article><b>12 connected applications</b><p>Reusable banking workflows across lending, payments, compliance and financial control.</p></article>
              <article><b>Built from scratch</b><p>Common platform patterns with configurable institution-specific workflows.</p></article>
              <article><b>Integration-ready</b><p>Designed to coexist with existing bank systems, payment rails and external services.</p></article>
              <article><b>Implementation-aware</b><p>Product ownership extended through validation, migration, deployment, training and support readiness.</p></article>
            </div>
          </aside>
        </div>
        <div class="ics-stat-grid" aria-label="Project evidence">
          <article class="ics-stat tone-blue"><strong>12</strong><b>applications built from scratch</b></article>
          <article class="ics-stat tone-violet"><strong>6 + 6</strong><b>two-phase product build</b></article>
          <article class="ics-stat tone-green"><strong>100+</strong><b>bank deployments · project claim</b></article>
          <article class="ics-stat tone-pink"><strong>25%</strong><b>manual AML/KYC compliance effort reduction</b></article>
        </div>
        <p class="ics-confidentiality">Confidential bank screenshots and proprietary production data are intentionally excluded. Product screens, reports, workflows, API examples and architecture visuals are original portfolio-safe reconstructions.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ics-section ics-ecosystem" id="ecosystem" aria-labelledby="ics-ecosystem-title">
      <div class="ics-inner">
        <div class="ics-section-heading">
          <div><p class="ics-overline">02 · Product ecosystem</p><h2 id="ics-ecosystem-title">Integrated Channels · Product Ecosystem</h2></div>
          <p>A digital banking platform for banks and NBFCs, built from scratch as a reusable 12-application suite. It standardises shared product patterns, controls and reporting while supporting institution-specific workflows, integrations with existing bank systems and operational readiness for implementation at client sites.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ics-ecosystem-layout">
          <aside class="ics-dark-panel ics-ecosystem-story">
            <span class="ics-overline">M2P FINTECH · INTEGRATED CHANNELS</span>
            <h3>One product foundation across twelve banking domains.</h3>
            <p>The suite connects domain applications through common platform patterns and configurable workflows.</p>
            <div class="ics-ecosystem-pillars">
              <span><b>12 applications</b><small>Product domains across the suite</small></span>
              <span><b>Common platform patterns</b><small>Shared controls and reporting</small></span>
              <span><b>Configurable workflows</b><small>Institution-specific journeys</small></span>
            </div>
          </aside>
          <div class="ics-ecosystem-board" aria-label="Twelve connected Integrated Channels Suite applications">
            <svg class="ics-ecosystem-lines" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 1000 600" preserveAspectRatio="none">
              <g fill="none" stroke="#8eb8e8" stroke-dasharray="7 7" stroke-width="2">
                <line x1="500" y1="300" x2="125" y2="75"/><line x1="500" y1="300" x2="375" y2="75"/><line x1="500" y1="300" x2="625" y2="75"/><line x1="500" y1="300" x2="875" y2="75"/>
                <line x1="500" y1="300" x2="125" y2="225"/><line x1="500" y1="300" x2="875" y2="225"/><line x1="500" y1="300" x2="125" y2="375"/><line x1="500" y1="300" x2="875" y2="375"/>
                <line x1="500" y1="300" x2="125" y2="525"/><line x1="500" y1="300" x2="375" y2="525"/><line x1="500" y1="300" x2="625" y2="525"/><line x1="500" y1="300" x2="875" y2="525"/>
              </g>
            </svg>
            {APPS.map((app, index) => <a class:list={['ics-eco-node', `ics-node-${index + 1}`]} href="#portfolio" data-open={app.id} style={`--app-tone:${app.color}`} aria-label={`Open ${app.name} product workspace`}><i>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</i><span><b>{app.name}</b><small>{app.category}</small></span></a>)}
            <div class="ics-ecosystem-hub"><small>M2P FINTECH · PRODUCT ECOSYSTEM</small><strong>Integrated Channels<br/>Suite</strong><span>12 applications · common platform patterns · configurable workflows</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="ics-section-note">Click any application to open its detailed Product Workspace.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ics-section ics-challenge" id="challenge" aria-labelledby="ics-challenge-title">
      <div class="ics-inner">
        <div class="ics-section-heading">
          <div><p class="ics-overline">01 · Product context</p><h2 id="ics-challenge-title">The problem was bigger than building 12 applications</h2></div>
          <p>Banks already operated within complex technology environments. The product therefore had to support domain-specific workflows while remaining configurable, integration-ready, migration-aware, controlled and implementable at client sites.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ics-challenge-grid">
          <article class="ics-dark-panel ics-challenge-story">
            <span class="ics-overline">The product challenge</span>
            <h3>One platform had to serve very different banking jobs.</h3>
            <p>Lending, AML, cards, reconciliation, treasury and audit do not share the same users or workflows. The product challenge was to find the reusable platform patterns without flattening the domain complexity.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Existing bank applications meant coexistence and integration mattered from day one.</li>
              <li>Client-specific workflows required configuration rather than a rigid one-size-fits-all product.</li>
              <li>Regulated processes required roles, validations, approvals, evidence, traceability and reporting.</li>
              <li>Legacy data required field mapping, transformation, validation and post-migration checks.</li>
              <li>Deployment success required training, documentation and L1/L2 support readiness.</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="ics-product-thesis">
            <span class="ics-overline">Product thesis</span>
            <h3>Standardise the platform. Configure the institution. Integrate the ecosystem.</h3>
            <p>The suite was approached as a common product foundation with modular domain applications—not as 12 disconnected projects.</p>
            <div class="ics-thesis-flow">
              <div><b>Standardise</b><span>Roles, controls, workflow patterns, reporting conventions.</span></div>
              <div><b>Configure</b><span>Institution-specific business rules and journeys.</span></div>
              <div><b>Integrate</b><span>Bank systems, payment rails and external services.</span></div>
              <div><b>Adopt</b><span>Migration, deployment, training and support.</span></div>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
        <div class="ics-response-grid">
          <article class="tone-blue"><b>Configure</b><span>Institution-specific journeys without rebuilding the product.</span></article>
          <article class="tone-green"><b>Integrate</b><span>Existing bank systems, payment rails and external services.</span></article>
          <article class="tone-pink"><b>Control</b><span>Roles, validations, approvals, evidence and traceability.</span></article>
          <article class="tone-amber"><b>Implement</b><span>Migration, deployment, training and support readiness.</span></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ics-section ics-strategy" id="strategy" aria-labelledby="ics-strategy-title">
      <div class="ics-inner">
        <div class="ics-section-heading">
          <div><p class="ics-overline">04 · Product strategy</p><h2 id="ics-strategy-title">From application list to a reusable banking product ecosystem</h2></div>
          <p>The strategy connected platform architecture, domain product design, implementation realities and client adoption. Each decision was intended to reduce repeated effort while preserving the flexibility banks needed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ics-strategy-grid">
          <article style="--tone:#9b8cf5"><i>01</i><h3>Common platform foundation</h3><p>Define reusable roles, permissions, workflow states, validations, reporting patterns and auditability before multiplying application complexity.</p></article>
          <article style="--tone:#73cbb4"><i>02</i><h3>Configurable institution model</h3><p>Separate reusable product behaviour from bank-specific configuration so workflows can adapt without turning every implementation into a new product.</p></article>
          <article style="--tone:#7eb5ed"><i>03</i><h3>Integration-first product design</h3><p>Identify systems of record, API contracts, authentication, failures, retries, reconciliation and hand-offs while journeys are being designed.</p></article>
          <article style="--tone:#efb785"><i>04</i><h3>Controls by design</h3><p>Translate business and regulatory requirements into roles, maker-checker patterns, approval states, validations, evidence and reports.</p></article>
          <article style="--tone:#f49dbd"><i>05</i><h3>Migration-aware product design</h3><p>Treat existing data as part of the product problem: assess, map, transform, validate, migrate and verify after migration.</p></article>
          <article style="--tone:#9dcbed"><i>06</i><h3>Two-phase roadmap</h3><p>Develop the first six applications during the initial six months, then select and build the remaining six using the foundation and learnings from phase one.</p></article>
          <article style="--tone:#a8d7a8"><i>07</i><h3>Feedback-led refinement</h3><p>Use progressive product demos, bank feedback, QA and UAT to refine workflows, reports, exceptions and implementation readiness.</p></article>
          <article style="--tone:#b6a7f0"><i>08</i><h3>Adoption as product outcome</h3><p>Carry product ownership through manuals, training, L1/L2 enablement, deployment readiness, production feedback and enhancement backlog.</p></article>
        </div>
        <div class="ics-decision-framework"><b>Decision framework used across applications</b><div>{['Problem', 'User / Role', 'Journey', 'Business Rule', 'Data', 'Integration', 'Exception', 'Report', 'Outcome'].map((item) => <span>{item}</span>)}</div></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ics-section ics-scope" id="pm-scope" aria-labelledby="ics-scope-title">
      <div class="ics-inner">
        <div class="ics-section-heading">
          <div><p class="ics-overline">05 · Product management scope</p><h2 id="ics-scope-title">End-to-end product leadership across strategy, build and adoption</h2></div>
          <p>The work extended beyond backlog management. It connected business discovery, product definition, technical solutioning, engineering execution, client validation, implementation and post-release enablement.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ics-ownership-grid">
          <article><span class="ics-pill">Strategy</span><h3>Vision, roadmap &amp; prioritisation</h3><p>Shaped the suite direction and phased roadmap.</p><ul><li>Product vision</li><li>6+6 sequencing</li><li>Dependencies</li><li>Prioritisation</li></ul></article>
          <article><span class="ics-pill">Discovery</span><h3>Problem &amp; requirement discovery</h3><p>Worked with SMEs, banks and compliance teams before development.</p><ul><li>Elicitation</li><li>Process mapping</li><li>Use cases</li><li>Edge cases</li></ul></article>
          <article><span class="ics-pill">Definition</span><h3>Product documentation</h3><p>Converted needs into executable product artefacts.</p><ul><li>BRD / FRD / FSD</li><li>API specs</li><li>Acceptance criteria</li><li>User manuals</li></ul></article>
          <article><span class="ics-pill">Design</span><h3>UX &amp; solution design</h3><p>Made workflows and architecture understandable across teams.</p><ul><li>Figma</li><li>DFD</li><li>ER mapping</li><li>Architecture diagrams</li></ul></article>
          <article><span class="ics-pill">Delivery</span><h3>Agile product execution</h3><p>Led backlog and sprint execution with engineering.</p><ul><li>Epics / stories</li><li>Refinement</li><li>2-week sprints</li><li>Daily sessions</li></ul></article>
          <article><span class="ics-pill">Quality</span><h3>Validation &amp; release readiness</h3><p>Connected product intent to QA and client acceptance.</p><ul><li>Feature testing</li><li>Edge cases</li><li>UAT</li><li>VAPT readiness</li></ul></article>
          <article><span class="ics-pill">Implementation</span><h3>Migration &amp; deployment</h3><p>Supported implementation at bank/client sites.</p><ul><li>Field mapping</li><li>Migration validation</li><li>Integration readiness</li><li>Production checks</li></ul></article>
