    <section class="ics-section ics-metrics" id="product-metrics" aria-labelledby="ics-metrics-title">
      <div class="ics-inner">
        <div class="ics-section-heading">
          <div><p class="ics-overline">06 · Product metrics</p><h2 id="ics-metrics-title">Prioritisation frameworks and product metrics used in regulated digital banking</h2></div>
          <p>These tools reflect realistic product-management practice for fintech and digital banking platforms, where decisions must balance customer value, regulatory criticality, implementation constraints and operational risk.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ics-metric-layout">
          <section class="ics-metric-panel ics-framework-panel" aria-label="Prioritisation frameworks">
            <h3>Prioritisation frameworks</h3>
            <div class="ics-framework-grid">
              <article><b>RICE</b><p>Prioritise regulated features by reach, impact, confidence and effort, particularly when deciding between onboarding improvements, AML controls, reconciliation workflows, or API enhancements across multiple bank implementations.</p></article>
              <article><b>MoSCoW</b><p>Separate must-have compliance and customer-critical workflows from should-have improvements so releases remain aligned to legal obligations, service continuity and migration readiness.</p></article>
              <article><b>Impact vs. Effort</b><p>Use this to sequence reusable platform capabilities such as workflow configuration, document upload, exception handling, and reporting dashboards across the product suite.</p></article>
              <article><b>WSJF</b><p>Apply weighted short-job-first thinking where business urgency, regulatory dependency and customer friction are combined into a single prioritisation view for roadmap decisions.</p></article>
            </div>
          </section>
          <section class="ics-metric-panel ics-health-panel" aria-label="Product metrics">
            <h3>Product metrics</h3>
            <div class="ics-health-grid">
              <article><b>Adoption Rate</b><p>Track percent of bank users or teams actively using a workflow after deployment.</p></article>
              <article><b>Transaction Success Rate</b><p>Measure successful completion of payments, lending actions, reconciliations, and operational flows.</p></article>
              <article><b>Exception Rate</b><p>Identify failed or manually worked cases requiring intervention across integrations and operational functions.</p></article>
              <article><b>STP Rate</b><p>Monitor straight-through processing for credit, payment, and compliance case handling.</p></article>
              <article><b>API Success Rate</b><p>Track the success of external calls to CBS, payment rails, credit bureaus and compliance services.</p></article>
              <article><b>Reconciliation Accuracy</b><p>Measure the percent of transaction records matching without manual adjustment or defect escalation.</p></article>
            </div>
          </section>
        </div>
        <div class="ics-usecase-metric"><span>PRODUCT → USE CASE → METRIC → IMPACT</span><p><b>Loan origination:</b> Application completion rate and turnaround time → reduced processing delays and better credit operations.</p></div>
        <section class="ics-priority-lens" aria-label="Portfolio-relevant decision lens">
          <div><span class="ics-overline">Portfolio-relevant decision lens</span><h3>Prioritisation across risk, impact and dependencies</h3></div>
          <article><b>Risk Reduction</b><p>Prioritise controls, alerting, validation and exception handling where compliance exposure and operational risk are highest.</p></article>
          <article><b>Customer / Business Impact</b><p>Weight improvements by effect on user experience, clearances, turnaround time and operational efficiency for banks, NBFCs and support teams.</p></article>
          <article><b>Dependency-based prioritisation</b><p>Sequence work according to external dependencies, data migration readiness, integration contracts and downstream approvals that can block delivery.</p></article>
          <article><b>Regulatory / Criticality-based prioritisation</b><p>Promote compliance, AML, KYC, audit and control functionalities ahead of low-risk enhancements when criticality and legal obligations justify it.</p></article>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>

